**The core issue**: The paper is a **solid proof-of-concept** on a semi-synthetic benchmark, but does not demonstrate practical utility on real-world data. The fundamental mismatch between the assumed causal graph and real-world data collection, combined with unreliable confounding detection and performance degradation on complexity, suggests the method may not scale beyond controlled, synthetic settings. This aligns with **reject** territory in the 3.5-5.0 range, but the strength of the methodological contribution (principled approach, thorough controlled evaluation) elevates it slightly.

